theorems.natural_language_statement:
Let $F$ be a finite field of cardinality $q$, let $\iota$ be a finite coordinate type of cardinality $n$, and let $\psi:F\to\mathbb C$ be a primitive additive character. For every word $c\in F^\iota$ and all $X,Y\in\mathbb C$,

$$
\sum_{v\in F^\iota}
X^{n-\operatorname{wt}(v)}Y^{\operatorname{wt}(v)}
\psi(\langle c,v\rangle)
=
\bigl(X+(q-1)Y\bigr)^{n-\operatorname{wt}(c)}
\bigl(X-Y\bigr)^{\operatorname{wt}(c)}.
$$

This identity packages the coordinatewise finite-field transform used in the complete- and Hamming-weight-enumerator identities as an independently reusable statement.

